index 0000000..a2caea5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SOLUTION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Solution
+
+Two bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:
+
+1. **`get` did not refresh recency.** The docstring says both `get` and `put`
+   count as "use", but a cache hit returned the value without moving the key to
+   the most-recently-used end of the `OrderedDict`. As a result, a recently
+   *read* key was still evicted as least-recently-used (failing
+   `test_get_refreshes_recency`). Fixed by calling
+   `self._data.move_to_end(key)` on a successful (non-expired) hit.
+
+2. **`put` evicted before checking for an existing key.** The capacity check
+   ran unconditionally, so updating a key already in a full cache first evicted
+   the least-recently-used *other* entry, even though the update adds no new
+   entry (failing `test_updating_existing_key_does_not_evict_others`). Fixed by
+   only evicting when `key not in self._data`.
